0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every practitioner screens before filing, and the screen starts with three qualifying buckets. Adam) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Cartabiano lays them out on the Ryan Downs show: a fully out-of-network event where the admit source) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (was the emergency room, an out-of-network charge on an in-network event, and emergency air ambulance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm ([0BGnlP4Q71M @ 00:00:23]. Cartabiano flags a common misperception. The rule is not limited to ED) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (patients; it turns on admit source. A patient who came through the ED and matriculated to observation or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (inpatient status still qualifies, and inpatient is where the big dollars come into play [0BGnlP4Q71M @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (00:00:40]. The second bucket drives most of the volume in the public CMS files: anesthesiologists, ED docs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (hospitalists, pathologists, radiologists and surgical groups. Team Health and SCP are named as the biggest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (private submitters [0BGnlP4Q71M @ 00:01:32]. K&L Gates partner Steve Pine maps the same perimeter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (from the statute side. It covers emergency services at an out-of-network facility including facility fees,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (emergency and non-emergency services by out-of-network providers inside in-network facilities, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (out-of-network air ambulance. Ground ambulance is excluded [VbqFYBvnpas @ 00:01:30]. CMS presenter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (Amanda Brander repeats the identical three triggers as step one of the pre-IDR sequence [7lzQt8aAlG0 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (00:03:30].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (The second consensus point is that plan funding decides the route, and getting it wrong ends the claim.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (Cartabiano splits the map into two kinds of states. Federal states push everything through the CMS process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (In bifurcated states, fully funded plans governed by the state Department of Insurance go to the state) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (process, while ERISA self-insured populations still follow the federal track [7lqb5ev54mA @ 00:00:20]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (instruction is blunt: read the insurance card or call the payer to confirm self-insured versus fully funded,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (because you'll get kicked out if you send it to the wrong place [7lqb5ev54mA @ 00:01:25]. Andres, CBO at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (Lido, has codified this fork in Lido's eligibility audit engine. A fully insured Texas plan goes to SB 1264) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (arbitration, and self-funded ERISA plans go federal. The team calls the full rule set quite complicated, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (is why they hard-coded it [NHWPEtUOyK0 @ 00:04:44]. Brander adds the detail that keeps volume federal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (Some states let self-funded plans opt into the state process, but nothing forces them to. The federal process) Tj ET
