BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 644.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 621.77 Tm (The costliest failure reported is the AMA's own war story. After Dr. C Chen's practice moved to a centralized) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 606.55 Tm (regional business office, accounts receivable lagged expected volumes; digging with the practice manager) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 591.32 Tm (revealed the office was leaning on a "payer matrix" instead of obtaining prior authorizations, and denied) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.10 Tm (claims were being charged off with no notification. "We eventually did get the problem fixed, but not before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.87 Tm (many thousands of dollars were lost," and the only signal that caught it was the AR report [Ie5ARcGEY1g @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 545.65 Tm (00:06:29]. RCM Mastery puts hard edges on the same trap: one wrong digit in a birth date is a guaranteed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 530.42 Tm (claim denial, and skipping pre-authorization on an MRI means a 100% denial [okx8geMd-gU @ 00:01:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.20 Tm (Etactics warns that attention skews toward coding, billing, denials and posting, which leaves the front end) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.97 Tm (that feeds them under-watched [M-Mz0m1tdrQ @ 00:00:33]. RCMOpsPro closes the loop on the cascade: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 484.75 Tm (patient-access failure turns into a mid-cycle coding problem and then a back-end cash-flow crisis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 469.52 Tm ([RddJn-tA3OM @ 00:01:52]. The lesson from Chen's office is blunt. Centralizing the business office did not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 454.30 Tm (centralize accountability, and the write-offs ran silently until someone read the receivables.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.07 Tm (The back-end traps are about sequence and integrity. Inlera University refuses to let anyone work AR before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.85 Tm (payment posting is caught up, posts by the EFT or bank-deposit date rather than whenever convenient, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 408.62 Tm (reconciles daily, weekly and monthly with the bookkeeper [RvLjKE1S1eU @ 00:25:58]. The same session) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 393.40 Tm (flags charge-poster bonuses as a fraud risk, sets audits at a 10% sample, and calls a modifier slapped on as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.17 Tm (a fix "abuse" [RvLjKE1S1eU @ 01:02:44]. Victoria at Contempo Coding warns that a paid claim is not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.95 Tm (clean bill of health: "oh well the claim got paid so that must mean it's okay because the insurance paid it not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 347.72 Tm (necessarily," with high volumes, high-dollar claims and modifier 25 drawing audits that can claw money back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 332.50 Tm ([pG2R1NwUlro @ 00:09:31]. Greg at Amazing Charts describes the owner-side version of the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 317.27 Tm (blindness: physicians who do not know their own biller's software and review no reports at all) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.05 Tm ([eKRUeJa5ZzQ @ 00:18:21]. The common failure is trusting the payment line. Posting lag, bonus-driven) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.82 Tm (charge entry and modifier fixes all look like revenue until reconciliation or a payer audit shows otherwise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 271.60 Tm (Inlera also warns against fee schedules set at 600% of Medicare.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.37 Tm (The economics checks start with three numbers that PayerWatch keeps apart. Ryan O'Hara defines gross) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.15 Tm (as what you charge, net as what you expect and cash as what you actually get, then walks a $1 billion gross) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.92 Tm (model down to $400 million net and $380 million cash; shifting just 2% of volume from commercial to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 210.70 Tm (uninsured is, in O'Hara's words, "over a million dollar a month impact to a place that's probably operating on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.47 Tm (pretty slim if not some month negative margins" [cePrn8Rhav8 @ 00:23:23]. The AMA puts the denial tax on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 180.25 Tm (the same ledger: unresolved denials average a $5 million annual loss, about 5% of net patient revenue, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.02 Tm (initial denial rates climbed from 9% to 12% between 2016 and early 2022 [Ie5ARcGEY1g @ 00:20:23]. On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.80 Tm (the cost side, Greg at Amazing Charts prices in-house billing for an internal medicine practice collecting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 134.57 Tm (about $310,000 a year, with salaries and benefits running about 77% of the billing cost and each statement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.35 Tm (costing about 50 cents plus labor [eKRUeJa5ZzQ @ 00:12:28]. UtreatiBill counters with outsourced pricing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 104.12 Tm (that "starts at just 2% with no heavy overhead or extra staff" [_0Dt6rewEvU @ 00:01:58]. Run payer mix,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 88.90 Tm (denial leakage and staffing cost before picking a vendor.) Tj ET
